<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    CURE GEOGRAPHY (spec §4). The owner's mechanic, replacing any caravan
    exemption: "desert and arid biomes, AND the salt ocean (ruled YES, round
    2: brine leaches the film), HALT slimification — desiccation or salt kills
    it. Severity in a drying biome doesn't just hold: it DECAYS."

    🔑 THE CURE GEOGRAPHY IS DATA, NOT CODE. This file adds one modExtension
    to four vanilla BiomeDefs. Any other mod tags its own biome the same way
    and the mechanic picks it up with no change here and no change in the C#:

      <modExtensions>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.DryingBiomeExtension">
          <decayPerDay>0.22</decayPerDay>
        </li>
      </modExtensions>

    The RUT campaign layer (§9) tags Ash'karr's deserts and its salt registers
    from its own side. Nothing here knows about them.

    ⚠️ A PATCH THAT MATCHES NOTHING LOGS NOTHING (CLAUDE.md). Each operation
    below is its own PatchOperationAdd against one named def, deliberately NOT
    a single xpath union — so a renamed or absent biome fails loudly as one
    unapplied operation instead of silently taking the other three with it.
    Ocean is `success="Normal"` like the rest: it exists in every install.

    ⚠️ THE DECAY RATE IS [INVENTED]. Spec §4: "full clear from stage 3 in
    ~4-5 days — slower than it grew; the walk must be earned." 0.22/day
    clears 0.9 severity in just over four days.

    ⚠️ THE OCEAN TAG IS MOSTLY FUTURE-PROOFING AND THE SPEC SAYS SO:
    "base-game caravans don't cross ocean tiles, so the tag is mostly
    future-proofing there." It matters for coastal maps and for any modded
    ocean travel. It is not dead weight, but do not expect to see it fire.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Desert"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <modExtensions>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.DryingBiomeExtension">
          <decayPerDay>0.22</decayPerDay>
        </li>
      </modExtensions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <modExtensions>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.DryingBiomeExtension">
          <!-- Bone-dry: fastest cure on the planet. -->
          <decayPerDay>0.30</decayPerDay>
        </li>
      </modExtensions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AridShrubland"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <modExtensions>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.DryingBiomeExtension">
          <!-- Dry, but not desert: the slowest of the four. -->
          <decayPerDay>0.14</decayPerDay>
        </li>
      </modExtensions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Ocean"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <modExtensions>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.DryingBiomeExtension">
          <!-- Not desiccation — brine. Ruled round 2. -->
          <decayPerDay>0.22</decayPerDay>
        </li>
      </modExtensions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
